            <ArticleTitle>Antinociceptive activity of Helicteres isora.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Helicteres isora root extracts were studied for antinociceptive activity on acetic acid-induced writhing test in mice, at a dose of 250 mg/kg. Petroleum ether, chloroform and aqueous ethanol extracts have shown significant activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
